    19	#    but they are ordered by visible anchor height: the upper-anchor family is A
    20	#    (receiver) and the lower-anchor family is B (donor). B never changes. A no longer
    21	#    turns into the whole B prototype; instead it keeps its own structure and receives B's
    22	#    two variable colors in two rounds. Because ARC supplies only one final output grid,
    23	#    the intermediate state is externalized by scale tier: scale-1 A sprites stop after
    24	#    round 1, while enlarged A sprites continue to round 2. Example:
    25	#      input:  A1, B1, A3, B2
    26	#      output: A1 gets only B's upper variable color; B1 stays B;
