    29	#    coexist in one output.
    30	# b) Complexity calibration:
    31	#    The rule uses only two visible axes: family identity (anchor high vs low) and size
    32	#    tier (prototype-sized vs enlarged). That keeps the branch count small enough to infer
    33	#    from 2-4 examples. We deliberately keep exactly two donor colors and exactly two
    34	#    receiver rounds, so the palette transfer is structured rather than free-form.
